    "result_text": "I implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py`, and both tests pass (the existing one and a new one I added).\n\n```python\nraw = client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n    model=MODEL, max_tokens=256, messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n)\nmessage = raw.parse()\nreturn {\n    \"request_id\": raw.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n    \"raw_body\": raw.text(),\n    \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n}\n```\n\n- **The body is read with `raw.text()`.** In the pinned anthropic 1.8.0, `text` is a method you call, not a property, so it has to be `raw.text()`. It returns the HTTP body exactly as the API sent it, not a copy rebuilt from the parsed message.\n- **The answer is built the same way as in `app/assistant.py`.** It joins the text blocks and skips any other block types.\n- **I added `tests/test_audit.py`.** It fakes the HTTP layer with the SDK's HTTP library (`httpx2`), so no real API call is made. It checks that the request ID comes from the header and that the body matches the returned JSON exactly. It also checks that the answer joins multiple text blocks, and that the request sends `max_tokens=256` and a single user message.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
